# Phase 36 Plan 07 (LIQ-01, D-28, R1-MEDIUM-4): the owner-run Liquipedia
# research spike (apps/api/scripts/liqSpikeProbe.ts) writes its JSON report
# to a path under apps/api/ via --out. That report holds RAW third-party API
# responses captured live from an owner-run spike, including editor revision
# metadata (`user`/`comment`) that has NOT yet been sanitized — it must never
# be committed as-is. The sanitized subset worth keeping as evidence reaches
# this repository ONLY through apps/api/src/liquipedia/__fixtures__/, added
# by hand with the corpus's existing sanitization rules applied (see
# apps/api/src/liquipedia/__fixtures__/MANIFEST.md). Dated variants are
# covered by the trailing glob so a re-run under a new filename is still safe.
apps/api/liq-spike-report*.json

# Phase 36 Plan 06 (SCL-01, D-20, D-28): the owner-run sparg0 real-data
# export (apps/api/scripts/sparg0Export.ts) writes exported PRODUCTION
# MATCH DATA to a path under apps/api/ via --out. This file must never be
# committed. Note that the pre-existing operator-output files under
# apps/api/ (gate6-*/enrichment-*/registry-*/migration-*.json) are
# untracked today by CONVENTION only — no rule covers them — so this block
# is deliberately the RULE, not a copy of that convention. Dated variants
# are covered by the trailing glob so a re-run under a new filename stays
# safe.
apps/api/sparg0-export*.json
apps/api/sparg0-export*.json.sha256
